  "body": "## Finding description and impact\nThe pairFor function in the Launchpad contract is as follows:\n```solidity\n    function pairFor(address factory, address tokenA, address tokenB) internal view returns (IUniswapV2Pair pair) {\n        (address token0, address token1) = sortTokens(tokenA, tokenB);\n        pair = IUniswapV2Pair(\n            address(\n                uint160(\n                    uint256(\n                        keccak256(\n                            abi.encodePacked(\n                                hex\"ff\",\n                                factory,\n                                keccak256(abi.encodePacked(token0, token1)),\n                                uniV2InitCodeHash // init code hash\n                            )\n                        )\n                    )\n                )\n            )\n        );\n    }\n```\nA snippet of the createPair function in the GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory contract is as follows:\n```solidity\n(address _launchpadLp, address _launchpadFeeDistributor) =\n    msg.sender == launchpad ? (launchpadLp, launchpadFeeDistributor) : (address(0), address(0));\n\nbytes32 salt = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(token0, token1, _launchpadLp, _launchpadFeeDistributor));\nassembly {\n    pair := create2(0, add(bytecode, 32), mload(bytecode), salt)\n}\n```\n\nIt can be observed that the salt calculation in Launchpad’s pairFor is:\n```solidity\nkeccak256(abi.encodePacked(token0, token1))\n```\nwhereas in the GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory contract, the salt is:\n```solidity\nkeccak256(abi.encodePacked(token0, token1, _launchpadLp, _launchpadFeeDistributor))\n```\nThis inconsistency leads to mismatched deployed pair addresses, which causes:\n\nThe _assertValidRecipient function in the Launchpad contract to fail.\n\nThe pair address calculated in the endRewards function of the Launchpad contract to be incorrect. As a result, this function can never be executed, and certain scenarios in the LaunchToken contract that depend on endRewards being called will be locked. For example:\n```solidity\nif (totalFeeShare == 0 && !unlocked) _endRewards();\n```\nThe above scenario may occur when a transfer of a certain LaunchToken happens to make totalFeeShare equal to 0.\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nEnsure that the salt calculation in both contracts is consistent.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {LaunchpadTestBase} from \"./LaunchpadTestBase.sol\";\nimport {ILaunchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/ILaunchpad.sol\";\nimport {Launchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/Launchpad.sol\";\nimport {LaunchToken} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchToken.sol\";\nimport {ERC20Harness} from \"../harnesses/ERC20Harness.sol\";\nimport {GTELaunchpadV2Pair} from \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\";\nimport {GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory} from \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory.sol\";\nimport {IUniswapV2Pair} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/IUniswapV2Pair.sol\";\nimport {IUniswapV2RouterMinimal} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/IUniswapV2RouterMinimal.sol\";\nimport {IUniswapV2FactoryMinimal} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/IUniswapV2FactoryMinimal.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\ncontract PoCSalt is Test {\n\n    bytes uniV2InitCodeHash = type(GTELaunchpadV2Pair).creationCode;\n\n   function setUp() public {\n\n   }\n    function test_submissionValiditySalt() external {\n        address tokenA =  makeAddr(\"A\");\n        address tokenB =  makeAddr(\"B\");\n        GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory factory = new GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory(address(1), address(2), address(3), address(4));\n        address pair1 = factory.createPair(tokenA, tokenB);\n        address pair2 = address(pairFor(address(factory), tokenA, tokenB));\n        assertNotEq(pair1, pair2, \"test fail\");\n    }\n\n    function pairFor(\n        address factory,\n        address tokenA,\n        address tokenB\n    ) internal view returns (IUniswapV2Pair pair) {\n        (address token0, address token1) = sortTokens(tokenA, tokenB);\n        pair = IUniswapV2Pair(\n            address(\n                uint160(\n                    uint256(\n                        keccak256(\n                            abi.encodePacked(\n                                hex\"ff\",\n                                factory,\n                                keccak256(abi.encodePacked(token0, token1)),\n                                uniV2InitCodeHash // init code hash\n                            )\n                        )\n                    )\n                )\n            )\n        );\n    }\n\n    function sortTokens(\n        address tokenA,\n        address tokenB\n    ) internal pure returns (address token0, address token1) {\n        if (tokenA == tokenB) revert(\"UniswapV2Library: IDENTICAL_ADDRESSES\");\n        (token0, token1) = tokenA < tokenB\n            ? (tokenA, tokenB)\n            : (tokenB, tokenA);\n        if (token0 == address(0)) revert(\"UniswapV2Library: ZERO_ADDRESS\");\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\nrun \n```shell\nforge test --match-test test_submissionValiditySalt\n```\nresult:\n```shell\nRan 1 test for test/c4-poc/PoCSalt.t.sol:PoCSalt\n[PASS] test_submissionValiditySalt() (gas: 5653587)\nSuite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 1.63ms (710.25µs CPU time)\n\nRan 1 test suite in 156.82ms (1.63ms CPU time): 1 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (1 total tests)\n```",
